.TH CYAML_LIST_REMOVE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cyaml_list_remove \- remove and free a list element by index
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cyaml.h>

ccol_retval_t cyaml_list_remove(cyaml seq, size_t index);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Remove the element at the position index from the list node seq.  The
function frees that element and all of its descendants recursively.  It
then shifts every element after index left by one position.  That shift
is O(n) in the number of elements after index.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success        - the function removed and freed the element.
ccol_invalid_args   - seq is NULL, seq is not CYAML_LIST, or index is
                      out of bounds.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_list_push (3),
.BR cyaml_list_get (3),
.BR cyaml_dictionary_remove (3)
